, two hours; outside study, six hours. Introduction to computer science via theory, applications, and programming. Basic data types, operators and control structures. Input/output. Procedural and data abstraction. Introduction to object-oriented software development. Functions, recursion. Arrays, strings, pointers. Abstract data types, object-oriented programming. Examples and exercises from computer science theory and applications. Letter grading.","url":"https://catalog.registrar.ucla.edu/course/2026/COMSCI31"},{"id":"COMPTNG 10A","title":"Introduction to Programming","units":"5","offered":[],"level":"lower","status":"active","in_major":true,"role":"required","groups":["Computing Specialization"],"column":0,"prereq_text":"","requires":null,"ambiguous":false,"description":"Lecture, three hours; discussion, two hours; laboratory, eight hours. No prior programming experience assumed. Basic principles of programming, using C&plus;&plus;; algorithmic, procedural problem solving; program design and development; basic data types, control structures and functions; functional arrays and pointers; introduction to classes for programmer-defined data types. P/NP or letter grading.","url":"https://catalog.registrar.ucla.edu/course/2026/COMPTNG10A"},{"id":"COMPTNG 10B","title":"Intermediate Programming","units":"4","offered":[],"level":"lower","status":"active","in_major":true,"role":"required","groups":["Computing Specialization"],"column":1,"prereq_text":"course 10A or Computer Science 31","requires":{"type":"or","items":[{"type":"course","code":"COMPTNG 10A","concurrent":false,"min_grade":null},{"type":"course","code":"COM SCI 31","concurrent":false,"min_grade":null}]},"ambiguous":false,"description":"Lecture, three hours; discussion, one hour; laboratory, eight hours. Object oriented programming in C++; operator overloading; memory management, copy and move constructors, copy and move assignment operators, destructors; iterators; data structures and their implementation, linked lists, binary search trees; inheritance and polymorphism; recursion, algorithms for sorting and searching. P/NP or letter grading.","url":"https://catalog.registrar.ucla.edu/course/2026/COMPTNG10B"},{"id":"COMPTNG 10C","title":"Advanced Programming","units":"5","offered":[],"level":"lower","status":"active","in_major":true,"role":"required","groups":["Computing Specialization"],"column":2,"prereq_text":"course 10B","requires":{"type":"course","code":"COMPTNG 10B","concurrent":false,"min_grade":null},"ambiguous":false,"description":"Lecture, three hours; discussion, two hours; laboratory, eight hours. More advanced algorithms and data structuring techniques; additional emphasis on algorithmic efficiency; advanced features of C&plus;&plus;, such as inheritance and virtual functions; graph algorithms. P/NP or letter grading.","url":"https://catalog.registrar.ucla.edu/course/2026/COMPTNG10C"},{"id":"POL SCI 6","title":"","units":"","offered":[],"level":"","status":"inactive","in_major":true,"role":"choice","groups":["Preparation for the Major: Political Science or Statisics"],"column":0,"prereq_text":"","requires":null,"ambiguous":false,"description":""},{"id":"SOCIOL 1","title":"","units":"","offered":[],"level":"","status":"inactive","in_major":true,"role":"required","groups":["Preparation for the Major: Sociology"],"column":0,"prereq_text":"","requires":null,"ambiguous":false,"description":""},{"id":"SOCIOL 20","title":"","units":"","offered":[],"level":"","status":"inactive","in_major":true,"role":"required","groups":["Preparation for the Major: Sociology"],"column":0,"prereq_text":"","requires":null,"ambiguous":false,"description":""},{"id":"SOCIOL 101","title":"","units":"","offered":[],"level":"","status":"inactive","in_major":true,"role":"required","groups":["The Major: Theory"],"column":0,"prereq_text":"","requires":null,"ambiguous":false,"description":""},{"id":"SOCIOL 102","title":"","units":"","offered":[],"level":"","status":"inactive","in_major":true,